# DATE FACTORY

## Git
Only `main` (existing `legacy-v1` may stay). Do not create branches.

## Donor
`донор` / `legacy` / «взять из донора» = read-only `../date_factory_legacy` (`legacy-v1`). Never edit it. Don't ask which donor.
Copy files + dependency closure into this repo; retarget `res://`. No links, submodules, or runtime paths to donor — the game must run if donor is gone.
Copy assets/helpers. Do not import old domain architecture (dating, girls, traits, bond, staff, crises, clone QA, legacy Game/save) unless asked. Prefer a simpler rewrite.

## How to implement
Do not only execute the literal ask. Analyze why it is needed, pick the best existing practice, and apply a mechanic already in the project. Assemble from ready systems; do not invent a parallel solution.

## Docs vs code
Documentation and code must match. Before implementing:
- Task is not in the docs → add it, then implement.
- Task is in the docs and matches the request → implement by the docs.
- Docs and request/code disagree → stop and tell the user; do not silently pick a side.

## User verifies
The user always checks the result. Agents do not play, screenshot, explore, `verify_project_runs`, or prove READY. Do not invoke `df-qa-worker` unless the user explicitly asks for QA.

## Playable, not compiled
Done = normal player route (enter, use, exit, save/load). Debug-only scenes and placeholders (capsules, void, debug UI, missing mats) are not a result. Broken loop → `NOT READY`.

## Scenes / look
Godot 4.7. Compact stylized low-poly, warm local light, no huge empty rooms. Reuse imported packs/GLB before modeling; check scale/pivot/collision; record new pack licenses.
Don't mass-reorder `.tscn`. After generating a scene, reopen it in Godot.

## Scope
No drive-by architecture, parallel frameworks, GDD changes, or content scale-up before a working POC.

## Subagents
If a subagent is Cursor Grok, use the latest Cursor Grok version available. Do not pin an older Grok.

## GodotIQ
Do not keep CORE in `AGENTS.md`, `.cursorrules`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.windsurfrules`, or copilot-instructions — MCP `serverUseInstructions` is enough. After `install-addon`, delete those injections. Keep `GODOTIQ_RULES.md` as on-demand full ref. Skip its play/screenshot/explore verification loops unless the user asks.
